 "preimage":
 "PROPOSED: SHA256(encodeParts ([\"seal.effect/v4-proposed-meta-all\", server, tool, compress(arguments)] ++ [meta-presence, compress(meta-object)-or-empty])) -> lowercase hex (64 chars)",
 "meta_presence":
 "_meta absence is framed as [\"meta.absent\", \"\"]; a present object is framed as [\"meta.present\", compress(object)], so absent and present-empty are distinct",
 "kernel_identity": "NOT part of the effect preimage (approval preimage only)",
 "integer_bound":
 {"rule":
  "an unquoted JSON number in guarded-call arguments carries at most 18 significant mantissa digits (10^18 < 2^63: fits i64 in the Stage-C twin) and at most 6 exponent digits; longer literals are rejected before hashing",
  "max_significant_digits": 18,
  "max_exponent_digits": 6},
 "encoding":
 "encodeParts: netstring framing — each part becomes '<charCount>:<part>', frames concatenated; hash input is the UTF-8 bytes of that string",
 "duplicate_keys":
 "a duplicate object key (raw text) or an escape sequence inside an object key anywhere in a tools/call line is a hard rejection before parsing",
 "absent_vs_null":
 "a tools/call with no arguments member hashes arguments = null (the 'null-arguments' vector); {} and {\"a\":null} are distinct effects"}
